    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't. This card's [When Attacking] effect is an effect that activates before your opponent blocks, therefore the activation timing has already passed by the time of the block timing.",
        "question": "This Digimon attacked the opponent player and was blocked by an opponent's Digimon that has more DP than this Digimon. Can I use this card's effect to digivolve into a level 6 Digimon card with [Leomon] in my hand, ignoring its digivolution requirements?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it can't. Only when this Digimon attacked a Digimon with higher DP at the time of the attack declaration can this card's [When Attacking] effect digivolve into a level 6 Digimon card with [Leomon] in your hand, ignoring its digivolution requirements.",
        "question": "This Digimon gained ＜Rush＞, it attacked the opponent player, and I used the ＜Rush＞ effect to switch the target of attack to an opponent's Digimon with higher DP than this Digimon. In such cases, can this card's [When Attacking] effect digivolve into a level 6 Digimon card with [Leomon] in my hand?",
        "reference": "[1]"
